able operation without requiring a camera.\nPreviously discussed approximate price was around $349, but that is historical reference only and should not be treated as a current shopping quote.\nEnhancia Neova\nRing-based musical gesture-control reference.\nRelevant historically because it showed that expressive hand motion can be translated into control data.\nMiMU Gloves / Glover\nStrong conceptual reference because MiMU treats body/hand movement as a programmable musical control interface.\nPotential output styles include:\n* MIDI;\n* OSC;\n* mapped gesture events.\nTornado A1 / other glove-style devices\nReferenced as possible wearable gesture-control examples.\nNo specific product was selected.\nCamera + MediaPipe\nImportant non-wearable alternative.\nCamera sees:\n* hand pose;\n* finger position;\n* gesture;\n* direction;\n* movement.\nThis could be useful as a proving-ground implementation before specialized hardware.\n⸻\n11. GESTURE NORMALIZATION MODEL\nA device should not directly emit things like:\n\"TURN MUSIC DOWN\"\nInstead, it should emit normalized physical state.\nExample:\n{\n  \"motion\": \"rotate\",\n  \"direction\": \"clockwise\",\n  \"amplitude\": 0.42,\n  \"velocity\": 0.31,\n  \"duration_ms\": 480,\n  \"confidence\": 0.96,\n  \"context\": \"right_hand\"\n}\nUseful normalized dimensions previously discussed:\n* motion type;\n* direction;\n* amplitude;\n* duration;\n* velocity;\n* confidence;\n* context.\nThen an interpreter can map:\nclockwise rotation\n+\ncurrent context = music\n→ raise volume\nor:\nclockwise rotation\n+\ncurrent context = seat selection\n→ move selection right\nSame gesture. Different context. No hardware lock-in.\n⸻\n12. WHY THIS MATTERS\nThe strongest conceptual insight is:\nReverse-engineer the interface, not the gadget.\nDon should not build the GCE around some specific ring, glove, MIDI controller, or mixer.\nInstead define:\nCONTROL EVENT CONTRACT\nThen allow many devices to satisfy it.\nPossible future inputs:\nDJ mixe